          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+programming"} functional programming
            using
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads+%28in+computer+science%29"} monads for computational effects
            %em monad transformers
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#Espinosa94"}> Espinosa 1994 §4
            ,
            = succeed "&rbrack;" do
              %a{:href => "#Espinosa95"} 1995 §2.6
          %p
            In practice this is typically motivated by and used for
            %em combining
            a monadic effect
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi new
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_{new}
            into any given one
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi new
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E} \mapsto \mathcal{E}_{new} \circ \mathcal{E}
            via a universal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+law"} distributive law
          %p
            Formally, a monad transformer on a given category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
            (of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/data+types"} data
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+endofunctor"} pointed endofunctor
            on the
            %a{:href => "monad#TransformationOfMonadsOnFixedCategory"} category of monads
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mnd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mnd(\mathbf{C})
            (this is made explicit in
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Winitzki22"} Winitzki 2022, p. 474
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo ↦
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E} \mapsto \mathcal{E}'
                taking monads to monads
            %li
              %p
                for each
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
                a
                %a{:href => "monad#TransformationOfMonadsOnFixedCategory"} morphism of monads
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi trans
                        %mi ℰ
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} trans_{\mathcal{E}} \,\colon\, \mathcal{E} \longrightarrow \mathcal{E}'
                (a
                = succeed ")" do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad+transformation"} monad transformation
            %li
              %p
                such that these are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural
                with respect to
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "monad#TransformationOfMonadsOnFixedCategory"} morphism of monads
          %p
            This construction is sometimes viewed (see
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#HP07"} HP07
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eff"} Eff
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theories"} Lawvere theories
          %h2#Details Details
          %p
            The following Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MonadTransformer"}
            is essentially the notion in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#LiangHudakJones95"} Liang, Hudak &amp; Jones 1995, left column of p. 339
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haskell"} Haskell
            (see the
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://hackage.haskell.org/package/transformers-0.5.6.2/docs/Control-Monad-Trans-Class.html#g:1"} Haskell Transformer class
          %p
          #PointedEndofunctorConditionOrNot.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              These authors, and the
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+programming"} functional programming
              = succeed "-community" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haskell"} Haskell
              = succeed "\u201D" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi trans
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mtext -
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} trans_{(\text{-})}
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:UnderlyingNaturalTransformation"} (1)
              — which they denote “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi lift
                    %mtext -
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} lift \text{-}
              ” — is not just a transformation between a single pair of monads, but a component a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+endofunctor"} pointed endofunctor
              on the whole category of monads. This further condition may be considered (or not) in addition to the following discussion.
          %p
          #MonadTransformer.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              Given monads
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}'
              on the same
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
              %em monad transformer
              between them is:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a system of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                #eq:UnderlyingNaturalTransformation.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi Type
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ⊢
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi trans
                          %mi D
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
